---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Denver's November 2026 Ballot" description="A plain-language guide to the measures on Denver's November 3, 2026 ballot - the Xcel franchise, civil service and auditor charter amendments, the two-year budget cycle, and the foie gras initiative." ogCategory="democracy">
  <section class="hero-mini">
    <div class="container">
      <h1 data-en="Denver's November 2026 Ballot" data-es="La Boleta de Denver de Noviembre de 2026">Denver's November 2026 Ballot</h1>
      <p data-en="Denver's coordinated election is November 3, 2026. Alongside the statewide races, city voters decide a 20-year utility franchise, two charter amendments that reshape how police discipline and city audits work, a change to how often Denver writes its budget, and the only citizen-initiated measure to qualify this year. Here is what each one does and where it touches our platform." data-es="La elección coordinada de Denver es el 3 de noviembre de 2026. Junto con las contiendas estatales, los votantes de la ciudad deciden una concesión de servicios públicos de 20 años, dos enmiendas a la carta que cambian cómo funcionan la disciplina policial y las auditorías de la ciudad, un cambio en la frecuencia con que Denver elabora su presupuesto, y la única medida de iniciativa ciudadana que calificó este año. Esto es lo que hace cada una y dónde se conecta con nuestra plataforma.">
        Denver's coordinated election is November 3, 2026. Alongside the statewide races, city voters decide a 20-year utility franchise, two charter amendments that reshape how police discipline and city audits work, a change to how often Denver writes its budget, and the only citizen-initiated measure to qualify this year. Here is what each one does and where it touches our platform.
      </p>
      <p class="hero-sublink" data-en="Also on this ballot: the at-large City Council special election. See the Council Candidate Tracker." data-es="También en esta boleta: la elección especial del Concejo Municipal en general. Consulta el Rastreador de Candidatos del Concejo.">
        Also on this ballot: the at-large City Council special election. See the <a href="/tools/candidate-tracker">Council Candidate Tracker</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Status banner -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <div class="status-banner">
        <p data-en="Ballot letters had not been published when this page was last reviewed in September 2026. Denver assigns letters (2A, 2B, and so on) to referred questions and numbers to initiated ordinances when the Clerk and Recorder certifies ballot content, and the official text arrives in the ballot information booklet mailed before the election. We describe each measure by subject until the letters are set. Denver Elections reports that eight municipal measures are headed to this ballot; the five below are the ones whose substance is on the public record so far." data-es="Las letras de la boleta no se habían publicado cuando esta página se revisó por última vez en septiembre de 2026. Denver asigna letras (2A, 2B, etc.) a las preguntas referidas y números a las ordenanzas iniciadas cuando la Secretaría Municipal certifica el contenido de la boleta, y el texto oficial llega en el folleto informativo que se envía antes de la elección. Describimos cada medida por tema hasta que se fijen las letras. Se reporta que ocho medidas municipales llegarán a esta boleta; las cinco a continuación son aquellas cuyo contenido consta en el registro público hasta ahora.">
          Ballot letters had not been published when this page was last reviewed in September 2026. Denver assigns letters (2A, 2B, and so on) to referred questions and numbers to initiated ordinances when the Clerk and Recorder certifies ballot content, and the official text arrives in the ballot information booklet mailed before the election. We describe each measure by subject until the letters are set. Eight municipal measures are reported to be headed to this ballot; the five below are the ones whose substance is on the public record so far.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Xcel franchise -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2 data-en="Xcel Energy Franchise Renewal" data-es="Renovación de la Concesión de Xcel Energy">Xcel Energy Franchise Renewal</h2>
        <p data-en="Referred by City Council, 10-2, on July 27, 2026. The biggest dollar figure on the ballot." data-es="Referida por el Concejo Municipal, 10-2, el 27 de julio de 2026. La cifra más grande de la boleta.">
          Referred by City Council, 10&ndash;2, on July 27, 2026. The biggest dollar figure on the ballot.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="measure-card">
        <div class="measure-header">
          <div class="measure-info">
            <h3 data-en="A 20-year franchise, through 2046" data-es="Una concesión de 20 años, hasta 2046">A 20-year franchise, through 2046</h3>
            <span class="measure-tag" data-en="Council-referred charter/franchise question" data-es="Pregunta de concesión referida por el concejo">Council-referred franchise question</span>
          </div>
          <span class="measure-badge measure-badge--money" data-en="~$180M/year" data-es="~$180M/año">~$180M/year</span>
        </div>
        <div class="measure-context">
          <h4 data-en="What It Does" data-es="Qué Hace">What It Does</h4>
          <ul>
            <li data-en="A franchise is the contract that lets Xcel run poles, wires, and gas lines in city streets and rights-of-way. Denver's current agreement expires December 31, 2026, and under the city charter a new one cannot take effect without voter approval. A yes vote grants Xcel the franchise through 2046." data-es="Una concesión es el contrato que permite a Xcel operar postes, cables y líneas de gas en las calles y derechos de vía de la ciudad. El acuerdo actual de Denver vence el 31 de diciembre de 2026, y según la carta municipal uno nuevo no puede entrar en vigor sin la aprobación de los votantes. Un voto a favor otorga a Xcel la concesión hasta 2046.">A franchise is the contract that lets Xcel run poles, wires, and gas lines in city streets and rights-of-way. Denver's current agreement <strong>expires December 31, 2026</strong>, and under the city charter a new one cannot take effect without voter approval. A yes vote grants Xcel the franchise <strong>through 2046</strong>.</li>
            <li data-en="The city puts the package at roughly $180 million a year in combined value: a 3% franchise fee worth about $34 million annually, roughly $10 million a year toward burying overhead power lines, and a one-time $2.5 million shareholder-funded contribution for bill assistance. The franchise fee is collected on customer bills and flows into the city's general fund." data-es="La ciudad calcula el paquete en aproximadamente $180 millones al año en valor combinado: una tarifa de concesión del 3% que vale unos $34 millones anuales, cerca de $10 millones al año para enterrar líneas eléctricas aéreas, y una contribución única de $2.5 millones financiada por accionistas para asistencia con las facturas. La tarifa de concesión se cobra en las facturas de los clientes y va al fondo general de la ciudad.">The city puts the package at roughly <strong>$180 million a year</strong> in combined value: a <strong>3% franchise fee</strong> worth about $34 million annually, roughly <strong>$10 million a year</strong> toward burying overhead power lines, and a one-time <strong>$2.5 million</strong> shareholder-funded contribution for bill assistance. The franchise fee is collected on customer bills and flows into the city's general fund.</li>
            <li data-en="This is the second attempt. Council rejected an earlier version 7-6 in August 2025, which sent the city back to negotiate and pushed the question past the 2025 ballot. Councilmembers Shontel Lewis and Sarah Parady cast the two no votes on referring the current deal." data-es="Este es el segundo intento. El concejo rechazó una versión anterior 7-6 en agosto de 2025, lo que devolvió a la ciudad a negociar y empujó la pregunta más allá de la boleta de 2025. Los concejales Shontel Lewis y Sarah Parady emitieron los dos votos en contra de referir el acuerdo actual.">This is the second attempt. Council <strong>rejected an earlier version 7&ndash;6 in August 2025</strong>, which sent the city back to negotiate and pushed the question past the 2025 ballot. Councilmembers <strong>Shontel Lewis</strong> and <strong>Sarah Parady</strong> cast the two no votes on referring the current deal.</li>
          </ul>
          <h4 data-en="Where It Touches Our Platform" data-es="Dónde Se Conecta con Nuestra Plataforma">Where It Touches Our Platform</h4>
          <ul>
            <li data-en="A franchise is the main leverage a city has over a monopoly utility, and a 20-year term sets the terms of Denver's energy transition past the city's own 2040 climate targets. Undergrounding money, rate advocacy, and any commitment to clean generation are negotiated here or not at all." data-es="Una concesión es la principal palanca que tiene una ciudad sobre un servicio público monopólico, y un plazo de 20 años fija las condiciones de la transición energética de Denver más allá de las metas climáticas de la ciudad para 2040. El dinero para enterrar líneas, la defensa de tarifas y cualquier compromiso con la generación limpia se negocian aquí o no se negocian.">A franchise is the main leverage a city has over a monopoly utility, and a 20-year term sets the terms of Denver's energy transition past the city's own 2040 climate targets. Undergrounding money, rate advocacy, and any commitment to clean generation are negotiated here or not at all. (See <a href="/platform/climate-environment">Climate &amp; Environment</a> and <a href="/platform/power-reliability">Power Reliability</a>.)</li>
            <li data-en="The bill-assistance piece is one-time and shareholder-funded, not a permanent affordability program, and the franchise fee itself is passed through to customers on their bills. Both are worth weighing against Xcel's rate increases." data-es="La parte de asistencia con las facturas es única y financiada por accionistas, no un programa permanente de asequibilidad, y la propia tarifa de concesión se traslada a los clientes en sus facturas. Ambas cosas merecen sopesarse frente a los aumentos de tarifas de Xcel.">The bill-assistance piece is <strong>one-time and shareholder-funded</strong>, not a permanent affordability program, and the franchise fee itself is passed through to customers on their bills. Both are worth weighing against Xcel's rate increases.</li>
            <li data-en="A no vote does not turn off the lights. It sends the city back to the table, as the 2025 rejection did, and keeps municipalization and shorter-term agreements on the table as alternatives." data-es="Un voto en contra no apaga las luces. Devuelve a la ciudad a la mesa de negociación, como lo hizo el rechazo de 2025, y mantiene la municipalización y los acuerdos de plazo más corto como alternativas.">A no vote does not turn off the lights. It sends the city back to the table, as the 2025 rejection did, and keeps municipalization and shorter-term agreements on the table as alternatives.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Civil service -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2 data-en="Civil Service Charter Amendments" data-es="Enmiendas a la Carta sobre el Servicio Civil">Civil Service Charter Amendments</h2>
        <p data-en="Referred by City Council. Changes the charter rules governing police and fire hiring, discipline, and command structure." data-es="Referida por el Concejo Municipal. Cambia las reglas de la carta que rigen la contratación, la disciplina y la estructura de mando de la policía y los bomberos.">
          Referred by City Council. Changes the charter rules governing police and fire hiring, discipline, and command structure.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="measure-card">
        <div class="measure-header">
          <div class="measure-info">
            <h3 data-en="Modernizing the Civil Service Commission" data-es="Modernizar la Comisión de Servicio Civil">Modernizing the Civil Service Commission</h3>
            <span class="measure-tag" data-en="Council-referred charter amendment" data-es="Enmienda a la carta referida por el concejo">Council-referred charter amendment</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="measure-context">
          <h4 data-en="What It Does" data-es="Qué Hace">What It Does</h4>
          <ul>
            <li data-en="Rewrites the charter provisions that govern the Civil Service Commission and the classified service for police officers and firefighters. The package removes the citizenship requirement for serving as a commissioner, revises disciplinary timelines, and adjusts probationary periods for officers and firefighters who take approved military or medical leave." data-es="Reescribe las disposiciones de la carta que rigen la Comisión de Servicio Civil y el servicio clasificado para policías y bomberos. El paquete elimina el requisito de ciudadanía para servir como comisionado, revisa los plazos disciplinarios y ajusta los períodos de prueba para oficiales y bomberos que toman licencia militar o médica aprobada.">Rewrites the charter provisions governing the <strong>Civil Service Commission</strong> and the classified service for police officers and firefighters. It removes the <strong>citizenship requirement</strong> for serving as a commissioner, revises <strong>disciplinary timelines</strong>, and adjusts <strong>probationary periods</strong> for officers and firefighters who take approved military or medical leave.</li>
            <li data-en="It also eliminates the charter-level caps on how many command staff positions the police and fire departments may have, moving that decision out of the charter and into the hands of the departments and the budget process." data-es="También elimina los límites a nivel de carta sobre cuántos puestos de personal de mando pueden tener los departamentos de policía y bomberos, sacando esa decisión de la carta y poniéndola en manos de los departamentos y del proceso presupuestario.">It also <strong>eliminates the charter-level caps</strong> on how many command staff positions the police and fire departments may have, moving that decision out of the charter and into the departments and the budget process.</li>
          </ul>
          <h4 data-en="Where It Touches Our Platform" data-es="Dónde Se Conecta con Nuestra Plataforma">Where It Touches Our Platform</h4>
          <ul>
            <li data-en="Disciplinary timelines are accountability infrastructure. Longer windows give investigators time to build a case; shorter ones protect officers from indefinite exposure. Read the actual timeline change before deciding, because the direction matters more than the word 'modernize.'" data-es="Los plazos disciplinarios son infraestructura de rendición de cuentas. Ventanas más largas dan a los investigadores tiempo para construir un caso; las más cortas protegen a los oficiales de una exposición indefinida. Lee el cambio real de plazos antes de decidir, porque la dirección importa más que la palabra 'modernizar.'">Disciplinary timelines are accountability infrastructure. Longer windows give investigators time to build a case; shorter ones protect officers from indefinite exposure. Read the actual timeline change before deciding &mdash; the direction matters more than the word "modernize." (See <a href="/platform/public-safety">Public Safety</a>.)</li>
            <li data-en="Dropping the citizenship requirement for commissioners opens civic service to immigrant Denverites, which is consistent with our position that residency, not immigration status, should define who participates in city government." data-es="Eliminar el requisito de ciudadanía para los comisionados abre el servicio cívico a los residentes inmigrantes de Denver, lo cual es consistente con nuestra posición de que la residencia, y no el estatus migratorio, debe definir quién participa en el gobierno de la ciudad.">Dropping the citizenship requirement for commissioners opens civic service to immigrant Denverites, consistent with our position that residency, not immigration status, should define who participates in city government. (See <a href="/platform/immigration-sanctuary">Immigration Sanctuary</a>.)</li>
            <li data-en="Removing command staff caps is a budget question wearing a governance costume: it makes it easier to add senior police and fire positions without returning to voters." data-es="Eliminar los límites del personal de mando es una cuestión presupuestaria disfrazada de gobernanza: facilita añadir puestos superiores de policía y bomberos sin volver a los votantes.">Removing command staff caps is a budget question wearing a governance costume: it makes it easier to add senior police and fire positions without returning to voters.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Auditor subpoena -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2 data-en="Auditor Subpoena Authority" data-es="Autoridad de Citación del Auditor">Auditor Subpoena Authority</h2>
        <p data-en="Referred by City Council. Would write the auditor's subpoena power into the charter." data-es="Referida por el Concejo Municipal. Escribiría en la carta el poder de citación del auditor.">
          Referred by City Council. Would write the auditor's subpoena power into the charter.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="measure-card">
        <div class="measure-header">
          <div class="measure-info">
            <h3 data-en="Subpoena power for audits and wage investigations" data-es="Poder de citación para auditorías e investigaciones salariales">Subpoena power for audits and wage investigations</h3>
            <span class="measure-tag" data-en="Council-referred charter amendment" data-es="Enmienda a la carta referida por el concejo">Council-referred charter amendment</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="measure-context">
          <h4 data-en="What It Does" data-es="Qué Hace">What It Does</h4>
          <ul>
            <li data-en="Codifies in the city charter the auditor's authority to subpoena records, for both performance audits of entities receiving city money and labor investigations such as wage theft and prevailing wage cases. The power currently rests on ordinance, which a future council can amend or repeal; the charter can only be changed by voters." data-es="Codifica en la carta municipal la autoridad del auditor para citar registros, tanto para auditorías de desempeño de entidades que reciben dinero de la ciudad como para investigaciones laborales como robo de salarios y casos de salario prevaleciente. El poder actualmente se basa en una ordenanza, que un concejo futuro puede modificar o derogar; la carta solo puede cambiarse por los votantes.">Codifies in the city charter the auditor's authority to <strong>subpoena records</strong> &mdash; both for performance audits of entities receiving city money and for labor investigations such as <strong>wage theft</strong> and prevailing wage cases. That power currently rests on ordinance, which a future council can amend or repeal; the charter can only be changed by voters.</li>
            <li data-en="The history is not hypothetical. Council granted the auditor subpoena power in 2021, repealed it during a dispute in 2022, and restored a version covering contractors and nonprofits in 2024. This measure would end that cycle by moving the authority out of reach of a single council vote." data-es="La historia no es hipotética. El concejo otorgó al auditor el poder de citación en 2021, lo derogó durante una disputa en 2022 y restauró una versión que cubre contratistas y organizaciones sin fines de lucro en 2024. Esta medida terminaría ese ciclo al poner la autoridad fuera del alcance de un solo voto del concejo.">The history is not hypothetical: council granted the power in <strong>2021</strong>, repealed it during a dispute in <strong>2022</strong>, and restored a version covering contractors and nonprofits in <strong>2024</strong>. This measure would end that cycle.</li>
          </ul>
          <h4 data-en="Where It Touches Our Platform" data-es="Dónde Se Conecta con Nuestra Plataforma">Where It Touches Our Platform</h4>
          <ul>
            <li data-en="Denver Labor, housed in the auditor's office, is the agency that enforces the city minimum wage and recovers stolen wages. An enforcement agency that cannot compel records is asking employers to volunteer evidence against themselves. This is the measure most directly tied to whether our wage policies mean anything in practice." data-es="Denver Labor, ubicada en la oficina del auditor, es la agencia que hace cumplir el salario mínimo de la ciudad y recupera salarios robados. Una agencia de cumplimiento que no puede exigir registros está pidiendo a los empleadores que ofrezcan voluntariamente pruebas en su contra. Esta es la medida más directamente ligada a si nuestras políticas salariales significan algo en la práctica.">Denver Labor, housed in the auditor's office, enforces the city minimum wage and recovers stolen wages. An enforcement agency that cannot compel records is asking employers to volunteer evidence against themselves. This is the measure most directly tied to whether our wage policies mean anything in practice. (See <a href="/platform/living-wage">$25 Minimum Wage</a>.)</li>
            <li data-en="It also strengthens oversight of contractors and nonprofits spending public money, which is the accountability side of every program we propose funding. The standing objections are due process and administrative burden on the entities subpoenaed." data-es="También fortalece la supervisión de contratistas y organizaciones sin fines de lucro que gastan dinero público, que es el lado de rendición de cuentas de cada programa que proponemos financiar. Las objeciones habituales son el debido proceso y la carga administrativa para las entidades citadas.">It also strengthens oversight of contractors and nonprofits spending public money &mdash; the accountability side of every program we propose funding. The standing objections are due process and administrative burden. (See <a href="/platform/government-transparency">Government Transparency</a>.)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Two-year budget -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2 data-en="Two-Year Budget Cycle" data-es="Ciclo Presupuestario de Dos Años">Two-Year Budget Cycle</h2>
        <p data-en="Referred by City Council. Sponsored by Councilmembers Amanda Sawyer, Shontel Lewis, and Stacie Gilmore as 'Budget Together Denver.'" data-es="Referida por el Concejo Municipal. Patrocinada por los concejales Amanda Sawyer, Shontel Lewis y Stacie Gilmore como 'Budget Together Denver.'">
          Referred by City Council. Sponsored by Councilmembers Amanda Sawyer, Shontel Lewis, and Stacie Gilmore as "Budget Together Denver."
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="measure-card">
        <div class="measure-header">
          <div class="measure-info">
            <h3 data-en="Optional biennial budgeting" data-es="Presupuesto bienal opcional">Optional biennial budgeting</h3>
            <span class="measure-tag" data-en="Council-referred charter amendment" data-es="Enmienda a la carta referida por el concejo">Council-referred charter amendment</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="measure-context">
          <h4 data-en="What It Does" data-es="Qué Hace">What It Does</h4>
          <ul>
            <li data-en="Lets Denver adopt a budget covering two years at a time instead of one, while keeping the option to return to annual budgeting when revenues are uncertain. The city currently writes a new budget every year, and finance officials warned in April 2026 that 2027 revenues are expected to stay flat." data-es="Permite que Denver adopte un presupuesto que cubra dos años a la vez en lugar de uno, manteniendo la opción de volver al presupuesto anual cuando los ingresos sean inciertos. La ciudad actualmente elabora un nuevo presupuesto cada año, y los funcionarios de finanzas advirtieron en abril de 2026 que se espera que los ingresos de 2027 se mantengan planos.">Lets Denver adopt a budget covering <strong>two years at a time</strong> instead of one, while keeping the option to return to annual budgeting when revenues are uncertain. Finance officials warned in April 2026 that 2027 revenues are expected to stay flat.</li>
          </ul>
          <h4 data-en="Where It Touches Our Platform" data-es="Dónde Se Conecta con Nuestra Plataforma">Where It Touches Our Platform</h4>
          <ul>
            <li data-en="A two-year cycle cuts the number of budget hearings in half, and budget hearings are where residents get their one scheduled chance to argue about city spending. It also gives longer planning horizons to programs that suffer from annual uncertainty, including rental assistance and shelter contracts. Which effect dominates depends on what participation the city builds into the off year." data-es="Un ciclo de dos años reduce a la mitad el número de audiencias presupuestarias, y las audiencias presupuestarias son donde los residentes tienen su única oportunidad programada de discutir sobre el gasto municipal. También da horizontes de planificación más largos a programas que sufren de incertidumbre anual, incluida la asistencia de alquiler y los contratos de refugios. Cuál efecto domina depende de qué participación construya la ciudad en el año intermedio.">A two-year cycle halves the number of budget hearings, and hearings are where residents get their one scheduled chance to argue about city spending. It also gives longer planning horizons to programs that suffer from annual uncertainty, including rental assistance and shelter contracts. Which effect dominates depends on what participation the city builds into the off year. (See <a href="/platform/participatory-budgeting">Participatory Budgeting</a> and <a href="/platform/fiscal-reform">Fiscal Reform</a>.)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Foie gras -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2 data-en="Prohibit Force-Feeding Birds Act" data-es="Ley para Prohibir la Alimentación Forzada de Aves">Prohibit Force-Feeding Birds Act</h2>
        <p data-en="Citizen-initiated ordinance from Pro-Animal Colorado - the only measure to reach this ballot by petition." data-es="Ordenanza de iniciativa ciudadana de Pro-Animal Colorado - la única medida que llegó a esta boleta por petición.">
          Citizen-initiated ordinance from Pro-Animal Colorado &mdash; the only measure to reach this ballot by petition.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="measure-card">
        <div class="measure-header">
          <div class="measure-info">
            <h3 data-en="Banning force-feeding and foie gras sales" data-es="Prohibir la alimentación forzada y la venta de foie gras">Banning force-feeding and foie gras sales</h3>
            <span class="measure-tag" data-en="Citizen-initiated ordinance" data-es="Ordenanza de iniciativa ciudadana">Citizen-initiated ordinance</span>
          </div>
          <span class="measure-badge measure-badge--petition" data-en="Qualified by petition" data-es="Calificó por petición">Qualified by petition</span>
        </div>
        <div class="measure-context">
          <h4 data-en="What It Does" data-es="Qué Hace">What It Does</h4>
          <ul>
            <li data-en="Prohibits the force-feeding of birds within Denver and bans the sale of products derived from the practice, including foie gras. Pro-Animal Colorado filed the petition in June 2025; the Clerk and Recorder certified the signatures as sufficient, putting it on the November 2026 ballot." data-es="Prohíbe la alimentación forzada de aves dentro de Denver y prohíbe la venta de productos derivados de esa práctica, incluido el foie gras. Pro-Animal Colorado presentó la petición en junio de 2025; la Secretaría Municipal certificó las firmas como suficientes, colocándola en la boleta de noviembre de 2026.">Prohibits the force-feeding of birds within Denver and bans the sale of products derived from the practice, including foie gras. Pro-Animal Colorado filed the petition in <strong>June 2025</strong>; the Clerk and Recorder certified the signatures as sufficient.</li>
          </ul>
          <h4 data-en="Where It Touches Our Platform" data-es="Dónde Se Conecta con Nuestra Plataforma">Where It Touches Our Platform</h4>
          <ul>
            <li data-en="Our platform takes no position on this measure. We include it because it is the only citizen-initiated ordinance that qualified this year, and because the petition process it used - gathering roughly 10,000 valid signatures to bypass City Council - is the same route any tenant, labor, or housing coalition would have to walk to put a policy on the ballot directly." data-es="Nuestra plataforma no toma posición sobre esta medida. La incluimos porque es la única ordenanza de iniciativa ciudadana que calificó este año, y porque el proceso de petición que usó - reunir aproximadamente 10,000 firmas válidas para eludir al Concejo Municipal - es la misma ruta que cualquier coalición de inquilinos, laboral o de vivienda tendría que recorrer para poner una política directamente en la boleta.">Our platform takes no position on this measure. We include it because it is the only citizen-initiated ordinance that qualified this year, and because the route it used &mdash; roughly <strong>10,000 valid signatures</strong> to bypass City Council &mdash; is the same one any tenant, labor, or housing coalition would have to walk to put a policy on the ballot directly.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How to vote -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <div class="vote-box">
        <h3 data-en="How to Vote in This Election" data-es="Cómo Votar en Esta Elección">How to Vote in This Election</h3>
        <ul>
          <li data-en="Election Day is November 3, 2026. Colorado mails a ballot to every active registered voter beginning about three weeks before Election Day; you can also vote in person or use a 24-hour drop box." data-es="El Día de la Elección es el 3 de noviembre de 2026. Colorado envía por correo una boleta a cada votante registrado activo comenzando unas tres semanas antes del Día de la Elección; también puedes votar en persona o usar un buzón de 24 horas."><strong>Election Day is November 3, 2026.</strong> Colorado mails a ballot to every active registered voter beginning about three weeks before Election Day; you can also vote in person or use a 24-hour drop box.</li>
          <li data-en="Colorado allows same-day voter registration. You can register or update your address through Election Day at a voter service center, though registering earlier is what gets a ballot mailed to you. Check your registration and find drop boxes at GoVoteColorado.gov." data-es="Colorado permite el registro de votantes el mismo día. Puedes registrarte o actualizar tu dirección hasta el Día de la Elección en un centro de servicio al votante, aunque registrarte antes es lo que hace que te envíen una boleta por correo. Verifica tu registro y encuentra buzones en GoVoteColorado.gov.">Colorado allows <strong>same-day voter registration</strong>. You can register or update your address through Election Day at a voter service center, though registering earlier is what gets a ballot mailed to you. Check your registration and find drop boxes at <a href="https://www.govotecolorado.gov" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GoVoteColorado.gov</a>.</li>
          <li data-en="Local measures sit at the bottom of a long ballot. Statewide races, congressional races, and judicial retention questions come first, and ballots that stop early are how city measures get decided by a fraction of the people who voted." data-es="Las medidas locales están al final de una boleta larga. Las contiendas estatales, las del Congreso y las preguntas de retención judicial vienen primero, y las boletas que se detienen antes de tiempo son la razón por la que las medidas municipales las decide una fracción de quienes votaron.">Local measures sit at the <strong>bottom of a long ballot</strong>. Statewide races, congressional races, and judicial retention questions come first &mdash; and ballots that stop early are how city measures end up decided by a fraction of the people who voted.</li>
          <li data-en="The at-large City Council special election is on this same ballot, and it has no runoff: whoever gets the most votes wins outright. See our Council Candidate Tracker for the ten candidates." data-es="La elección especial del Concejo Municipal en general está en esta misma boleta, y no tiene segunda vuelta: quien obtenga más votos gana directamente. Consulta nuestro Rastreador de Candidatos del Concejo para ver los diez candidatos.">The at-large City Council special election is on this same ballot, and it has <strong>no runoff</strong>: whoever gets the most votes wins outright. See our <a href="/tools/candidate-tracker">Council Candidate Tracker</a> for the ten candidates.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
